# 122.md — every text file is stored AND checked out with LF on every platform.
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh clone or worktree
# there materialised the whole tree with CRLF. Four unit-test files then fail for
# reasons unrelated to the code under test: three import .mjs scripts that begin
# with a `#!` line (the Vitest transform only recognises a hashbang ending in LF)
# and one matches multi-line source text. Long-lived working trees hid this
# because files written by editors and tools keep LF. All blobs are already LF, so
# this line changes no file content; it only removes the per-machine difference.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows command scripts must keep CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses labels.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The Postgres schema + its migrations are GENERATED by
# server/scripts/sync-postgres-schema.mjs, and tests/unit/postgres-schema-sync.test.js
# compares the generator's output (always LF) against the bytes on disk. On Windows a
# plain checkout materialises them with CRLF, so the drift test fails on a clean tree
# for a reason that has nothing to do with the schema. Pin these to LF so the
# generator and the working copy can agree.  (116.md validation)
server/prisma/postgres/*.prisma text eol=lf
server/prisma/postgres/migrations/**/*.sql text eol=lf
